WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.073
- Are you scared to do it

00:00:01.073 --> 00:00:03.340
because your parents won't like it?

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.240
- No, my parents actually support me--

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.420
- Okay, so what are
you afraid of, failing?

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:08.630
- Not failing... but...

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.650
Still being at the same place,

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.660
when my friends are at the next level.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:15.850
- Huge mistake.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.960
You don't want the same
things your friends want.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.923
So why the fuck do you
care what they have?

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.160
The biggest reason people

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.050
are unhappy right now,

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.640
is 'cause they value
somebody else's opinion

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.580
more than they value their own.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.990
Have the conversation

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.890
with the person that's holding you back.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.810
The reason most people who
are listening right now

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.460
are not doing that thing,

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.511
is they're worried about
the opinion of somebody.

00:00:35.511 --> 00:00:37.050
(echoing)

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.950
I am so devastated that you actually let

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.104
your grandma's point of view,

00:00:41.104 --> 00:00:43.860
your mom, your dad, you
sister, your aunt...

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.260
You still let somebody else dictate based

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:47.740
on their opinion.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.641
Every action you do, and it's your life.

00:00:50.641 --> 00:00:52.960
(clock ticking)

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.760
The reason I'm super happy,

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.860
is nobody can tell me nothin'.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.620
My wife, mom, and daughter,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.150
could walk into my room right now,

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.630
tell me I'm a piece of crap,

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.780
and I would be 100% un-phased.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.363
That is some gangster emotional structure.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:12.380
If you're not feelin'
it, find new friends.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.720
I'm being dead serious about this.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.450
This one is real big for me.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.052
The only way I've seen,

00:01:17.052 --> 00:01:20.350
now that I'm older, that
you can build confidence,

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:21.760
is if you surround yourself

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.410
with people who are optimistic.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:26.770
Start trimming your friend group,

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.880
and start adding to your friend group,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.840
predicated, on what you wanna be.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.220
Like, it's unbelievable
what happened to me

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.220
when I got into the Silicon Valley world,

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.160
and started meeting like, Mark Zuckerberg,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.940
and like, Ed Williams and--

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:39.773
like, Travis--

00:01:39.773 --> 00:01:42.070
